cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use scQC in your work, please cite it."
title: "scQC: a reproducible quality-control pipeline for single-cell and single-nuclei RNA-seq"
abstract: >-
  scQC separates deriving quality-control thresholds from applying them. Every parameter
  carries a class recording whether it was fixed by the pipeline, derived from the data,
  declared in advance, or adjudicated by a human, and every removal requires a recorded
  approval and remains recoverable.
authors:
  - family-names: Lin
    given-names: Jiaen
    email: jiaenlin999@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/JiaenLin/scQC"
license: MIT
type: software
keywords:
  - single-cell RNA-seq
  - single-nuclei RNA-seq
  - quality control
  - reproducibility
  - ambient RNA
  - doublet detection
